<title>USA: Consulier sees lower 1997 earnings.</title>
<headline>Consulier sees lower 1997 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TEQUESTA, Fla. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consulier Engineering Inc said Friday  it sees reduced 1997 earnings because of expenses related to its new  subsidiary, C-6 Products Inc.</p>
<p>The company said it is projecting reduced earnings of $0.02 per share  for the second and third quarters and $0.10 for the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>It estimates year-end income will be reduced by $370,000, or $0.14  per share to $425,000.</p>
<p>C-6 Products was formed to produce and market the Tool Topper products  and hand-held powered hacksaw.  Consulier previously announced it  acquired the rights to the products.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately able to provide financial information  on the acquisition.</p>
</text>
